                     identity in 867 aa overlap) and TR:O86674 (EMBL:AL031371)
                     (90.8% identity in 370 aa overlap) which together
                     constitute a single hypothetical protein split across the
                     join between S.coelicolor cosmids 1F2 and 4G2. It has very
                     weak similarity to DNA methylases, which combined with the
                     presence of a DNA methylases signature and possible
                     DNA-binding region (helix-turn-helix) provides
                     circumstantial evidence of DNA-methylase function. The
                     central third of the CDS is relatively AT rich. Contains
                     probable helix-turn-helix motif at aa 38-59 (Score 1036,
                     +2.72 SD). Contains PS00092 N-6 Adenine-specific DNA
                     methylases signature"
